      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks.  I see these had to diverge quite a bit from the upstream commits.  Perhaps it would be easier to backport arm64 support for `scoped_ksimd()` itself?  I assume you didn\u0027t do that already because the upstream code doesn\u0027t support direct access to `kernel_neon_begin()` and `kernel_neon_end()` anymore, i.e. *all* callers of them had to be converted to `scoped_ksimd()`.  However, for the backport, we could actually support both ways.  The `ksimd` lock guard would just call the underscored functions `__kernel_neon_begin(_T-\u003elock)` and `__kernel_neon_end(_T-\u003elock)`, which are the equivalent of the non-underscored functions upstream.  With that, we\u0027d be able to backport arm64 code that uses `scoped_ksimd()` as-is, while still being able to keep code that doesn\u0027t use it.",
